REMARK   1 PROTEON ORACLE FIXTURE - PDBFixer-prepared crambin (1crn) for AMBER96.
REMARK   1
REMARK   1 PRODUCER   PDBFixer 1.12.0 / OpenMM 8.5.2
REMARK   1 SOURCE     test-pdbs/1crn.pdb
REMARK   1 PREP       findMissingResidues (cleared), replaceNonstandardResidues,
REMARK   1            removeHeterogens(keepWater=False), addMissingHydrogens(pH 7.0)
REMARK   1 CREATED    2026-08-27
REMARK   1
REMARK   1 WHY THIS FILE IS COMMITTED RATHER THAN REGENERATED:
REMARK   1 PDBFixer.addMissingHydrogens is NOT deterministic across runs. Three
REMARK   1 successive preparations of 1crn.pdb produced three different sets of
REMARK   1 hydrogen coordinates (642 atoms each time, differing positions), which
REMARK   1 moves single-point energies by tens of kJ/mol. Any frozen oracle
REMARK   1 reference value must therefore be pinned to a fixed structure. Engines
REMARK   1 compared against each other WITHIN one run may prepare on the fly;
REMARK   1 tests that assert stored numbers must load this file.
REMARK   1
REMARK   1 Regenerate only if the prep protocol itself changes, and re-measure
REMARK   1 every frozen value that references it (tests/oracle/test_molly_energy.py).
REMARK   1 CREATED WITH OPENMM 8.5.2, 2026-08-27
